*   Tempo & Pulse: 62–78 BPM. A heavy, syncopated hydraulic drag characterized by swung half-time kicks, unquantized rimshots struck against sheet-metal ducts, and off-beat pickaxe strikes creating an unsteady, claustrophobic groove.
*   Harmonic Palette: Phrygian dominant and double-harmonic minor scales colliding with lush, detuned vaporwave major-seventh and minor-ninth chord progressions; chords frequently melt, droop in pitch, and slip into microtonal dissonance.
*   Production Signatures: 
    1. Borehole Convolving: Drums and synthesizers are processed through extreme, zero-damping convolution reverbs sampled inside 2,000-meter vertical ventilation tubes.
    2. Fuzz-Oboe Octave Tracking: The oboe is fed through germanium fuzz circuits, tape delays, and sub-octave generators to create a ghostly, brassy, multi-timbral wail.
    3. Firedamp Tape Degradation: Master tracks are deliberately printed to oxidized cassette tape and exposed to artificial heat and humidity modulation, producing seasick wow-and-flutter and sudden, spectral high-frequency dropouts.
*   Dynamics: Suffocating, whisper-quiet ambient passages of dripping water, distant radiator hiss, and breathy oboe multiphonics that abruptly detonate into blinding, tectonic walls of fuzz-saturated acid guitars and deafening pipe-hammering.

